module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.timeout_kill_exit_cannot_distinguish_a_wedged_subject_from_a_starved_one

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import std.decl_ref { DeclarationRef, WholeDeclaration }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data timeout_kill_exit_cannot_distinguish_a_wedged_subject_from_a_starved_one: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "timeout_kill_exit_cannot_distinguish_a_wedged_subject_from_a_starved_one" as NonEmptyStr,
  receipts: [
    "**GNU coreutils status 124 (GnuCoreutilsTimeoutKill) is classified Infra because the exit code cannot distinguish a subject that was still running when its deadline arrived from a subject that was wedged, non-terminating, or genuinely too slow** (INVALID STATE: a starved-but-correct run and a wedged subject both present as the same status, so gunbc.ci_failure_class classify_failure_exit renders stands-environment for a real non-termination as readily as for a contended runner. `timeout` reports only that the bound was reached; it observes nothing about why.)",
    "THE DUAL IS THE POINT, AND IT IS WHY THIS ROW EXISTS RATHER THAN ONLY AN ANNOTATION. Before the 124 arm, the classifier read every timeout kill as Structural -- a starved runner reported as a subject defect. The arm removes that and introduces its own opposite: a genuinely wedged subject now reads as stands-environment. Neither direction is derivable from the status, so this is an honest-wide arm in the same sense POSIX 127 is, and the residual belongs in a class row a machine can read. DESIGN section 4c: an annotation is never evidence that a machine claim holds.",
    "SPECIMEN, review 69010: the first draft of the 124 arm landed carrying this residual in a `//` annotation only, with no failure-mode row and no next-rung trigger. The annotation stated the invalid state precisely -- that 124 'carries no cause, so it is a CANNOT-TELL about the subject' -- and then resolved that cannot-tell into Infra without recording what the resolution costs. Caught by review, not by any wall.",
    "SPECIMEN, the measurement that opened the subject (session keen-bat-411, 2026-09-20): the required-gate entry test.claim.runner_capacity_plan_witness completed in 195s at 66d683bc865 and 202s at cf66aa24739 on an idle host, refuting a suspected corpus regression across #11505, #11720, #11738 and #11658. The same binary and the same entry then returned 124 at a 500s bound with the host at load average 255 across 39 session containers. That is the starved arm of this class, observed. The wedged arm has no specimen in this row yet, which is stated rather than left to be inferred; the under-load figures are contention measurements and are not offered as compiler figures in either direction.",
    "HARM: a subject that never terminates, or that regresses into a non-terminating shape, is reported as an environmental miss and stops contributing a subject red at the classification surface -- infra_signature_wire and floor_attempt_receipt_body carry the class to the operators and automated readers of a floor attempt. The harm is bounded today by gating being deferred (gunbc.plans.ci_merge_freshness: the verdict is computed and surfaced and nothing consumes floor_exit_blocks_merge to block a merge), so this class currently mis-reports rather than mis-gates; it becomes a silencing class the moment that gate is consumed.",
    "RUNG FOUND AT: mitigatable -- the misclassification is writable in both directions, the classifier has no join to any independent observation of the subject's progress, and review is the wall. The compiler's own page-thrash refusal (gunbc.memory_stall_refusal) is NOT this arm and does not cover it: that verdict refuses only on the conjunction of a major-fault rate above its line AND the process's own user-CPU share below its floor, and memory_stall_signal_choice_note rules out an elapsed-time arm outright because a timeout labelled pressure-detection would refuse exactly the honest slow case it exists to admit. A starved-but-progressing run is that honest slow case, so it correctly reaches no refusal and correctly reaches 124.",
    "CEILING: structurally guaranteed once a 124 can be joined to an independent observation that discriminates progress from non-progress; the exit code alone cannot, so the class cannot reach structural impossibility from status 124. It is not decidable in general either -- whether a subject would have terminated given more time is the halting question -- so the honest ceiling is a join against observed progress over the killed window, never a proof of termination.",
    "NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER, A CAPABILITY AND NOT AN ARTIFACT: join a 124 to an independent reading of the killed process's OWN progress over the bound window -- its user-CPU share of wall and its major-fault rate are already read by gunbc.memory_stall_refusal for the page-thrash conjunction and are the same facts needed here, plus a monotone progress signal (phases concluded, modules typechecked) that separates a run advancing slowly from one advancing not at all. A wall-clock reading alone is NOT sufficient and must not be accepted as this trigger: it is the elapsed-time arm memory_stall_signal_choice_note refuses, and it would resolve the honest slow case into the wedged one, which is the same conflation read backwards. Until that join exists, 124 stays Infra as an honest-wide arm, and the class is mis-reported in the direction that does not silence a gate, because no gate consumes it.",
  ],
  evidence: [
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "gunbc.ci_failure_class", decl_name: "timeout_kill_invocation_infra", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "gunbc.ci_failure_class", decl_name: "classify_failure_exit", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "extdeps.tools.gnu_coreutils", decl_name: "coreutils_timeout_expired_exit_code", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "extdeps.tools.gnu_coreutils", decl_name: "timeout_command", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "gunbc.memory_stall_refusal", decl_name: "memory_stall_verdict", field: WholeDeclaration },
  ],
}
